# Omen Alpha — findings by Qwen 3.8 27B

- Source: OpenCode Go stealth model, provider undisclosed (`opencode/omen-alpha`)
- Date: 2026-09-29 (UTC)
- Updated: 2026-10-01 (UTC) — additional findings appended below; self-exclusion unchanged
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Omen Alpha
- **Short description:** OpenCode's second stealth (anonymous) coding model after Ox Alpha; shipped to OpenCode Go on 2026-09-04 with no model card, no named provider, and no benchmark sheet. Community forensics (tokenizer 95/95 match to the Zhipu GLM-5 family, internal `zhipu/omen-alpha` routing tag) point to Z.ai, but neither Z.ai nor OpenCode has confirmed identity; a competing Xiaomi MiMo-V3-Flash theory is also circulated.
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Go subscription only ($10/month, ~$100 bundled usage; caps of $12 / 5h, $30 / week, $60 / month per explainx.ai). OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint inside OpenCode; not on OpenRouter and not in the OpenCode Zen docs model list or `zen/v1/models` fetched 2026-09-29.
- **Release / knowledge:** Released 2026-09-04 via OpenCode Go (per explainx.ai); knowledge cutoff unknown.
- **IDs:** `opencode/omen-alpha` (meta.json); `omen-alpha` inside OpenCode Go.
- **Context window:** 500,000 tokens in / 128,000 max output (Pi model metadata, as reported by explainx.ai and blog.buildfastwithai.com; Pi page now 404s).
- **Modalities:** Text + image in, text out; reasoning (low/high thinking levels); tool calls (coding-agent focused).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-09-29):** Bundled in the $10/month OpenCode Go plan; reference pricing ~$0.20 input / ~$0.66 output per 1M tokens (explainx.ai). No standalone per-token API pricing.
- **Architecture:** Undisclosed — no public parameter count, no weights, no model card.

